# CI after push

When this agent pushes to `origin` (or completes a user-requested push):

1. Confirm `gh auth status` works (Windows fallback:
   `C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe`).
2. List runs: `gh run list --limit 5` from the repository root.
3. Watch the run for the pushed commit/branch: `gh run watch` or poll until not
   `in_progress`.
4. On failure: `gh run view <run-id> --log-failed`, diagnose, fix, push again,
   repeat until all required jobs pass.
5. Tell the user the run URL or conclusion; do not leave verification to them
   by default.

Local Makefile targets (`make lint-api`, tests, etc.) run before push; `gh`
confirms what ran on GitHub.
